# Production environment variables — set these in Railway's Variables dashboard
# These are NOT committed with real values — just documentation of required keys

# Get this from: Railway → API service → Settings → Networking → Public Domain
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://YOUR-API-SERVICE.up.railway.app

# Same as above (WebSocket uses same origin)
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=https://YOUR-API-SERVICE.up.railway.app

# ── How to fix ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED / DNS_PROBE_FINISHED_NXDOMAIN ─────────────
#
# If the Railway API domain stops resolving:
# 1. Railway dashboard → API service → Settings → Networking
# 2. Click "Generate Domain" to create a new *.up.railway.app URL
# 3. Update NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL here AND in Railway → Web service → Variables
# 4. Redeploy the web service
#
# PERMANENT FIX: Use a custom domain (api.yourdomain.com) via Cloudflare CNAME
# pointing to your Railway service — this never changes even if Railway regenerates.
